%% What it shows: the desk agent as a LangGraph graph with a review step. The state (the messages) enters at START;
%% the model node calls the model; our route reads the reply; lookups go to the tools node and back to the model;
%% a refund request goes to the review node, where interrupt() stops the run until a person decides.
%% Ink: what the model does. Lime: what our own code does. Dashed: the checkpointer, which saves the state after every step.
%% Export: npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i desk_graph_with_review.mmd -o desk_graph_with_review.png -b white -s 2
flowchart LR
    start([START<br/>state in:<br/>messages]) --> model[model node<br/>one call to the model;<br/>adds its reply]
    model --> route{route:<br/>what does the<br/>reply ask for?}
    route -->|a lookup| tools[tools node<br/>runs each tool call;<br/>adds the results]
    route -->|a refund request| review[review node<br/>interrupt: the run stops<br/>and waits for a person]
    route -->|no tool| finish([END<br/>state out: messages,<br/>the answer is the last one])
    review -->|approve| tools
    review -->|reject, with a reason| model
    tools -->|back edge| model
    saver[(checkpointer:<br/>saves the state after<br/>every step, per thread id)] -.- review
    classDef model fill:#0B1220,color:#FFFFFF,stroke:#0B1220
    classDef code fill:#C9F24D,color:#0B1220,stroke:#0B1220
    classDef note fill:#FFFFFF,color:#0B1220,stroke:#6B7383,stroke-dasharray:5 4
    class model model
    class route,tools,review code
    class saver note
